WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.936
In the spring of 1918,
the Ottoman army marched east.

2
00:00:06.976 --> 00:00:09.426
Three columns pushed toward Yerevan:

3
00:00:09.466 --> 00:00:14.268
past Sardarapat, through Bash Abaran,
and toward Karakilisa.

4
00:00:14.628 --> 00:00:16.518
Behind the thin Armenian front

5
00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:19.218
were the last Armenian lands
of the Caucasus,

6
00:00:19.258 --> 00:00:23.410
and hundreds of thousands
of refugees from the Genocide.

7
00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:26.960
General Movses Silikyan
gathered what he had:

8
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.580
Armenian regiments, volunteers,
refugees and villagers,

9
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.422
and the Yazidi horsemen
of Jangir Agha.

10
00:00:34.462 --> 00:00:38.152
Tradition holds that the Catholicos
had the church bells rung

11
00:00:38.192 --> 00:00:39.992
to call the people to battle.

12
00:00:40.301 --> 00:00:44.011
On 22 May the Armenians
counterattacked beneath Ararat,

13
00:00:44.051 --> 00:00:47.699
and over the next days drove
the Ottoman troops back.

14
00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:52.192
Taken together, the May battles
stopped the Ottoman drive on Yerevan.

15
00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:55.162
On 28 May 1918,

16
00:00:55.202 --> 00:00:57.886
the First Republic
of Armenia was born.

17
00:00:58.246 --> 00:01:00.493
Not one step back.

